OLD 11 (all scanned for machine-only AI(W906-*) tags / W906_ / Msk / s_ / k* identifiers missing from the laptop copy: 0): Ifor01 IT-1 batches 2-3 (MyTempPanel.cpp/.h, uTemp_Set.cpp per golden), build_nonoracle.bat (Ninja when found; a dir with a CMakeCache keeps its generator, so build_integ_dbg_x86 is unchanged), tools/wave_wrapup_gate.ps1, docs x3, web HMICLOSE (background.html, page/ht9045_main_close.js, page/ht9045_recipe_client.js -- in the web commit). NEW 3: tests/test_it1_mytemppanel.cpp, tests/test_it1_utempset.cpp, tools/ninja_setup.ps1. Motor/myGALILmotor.cpp and Motor/mymotor.cpp merged = the machine's (the package carries the machine's own IDX1203); tests/CMakeLists +2 tests, no duplicate registration.
Two conflicts kept the machine side: MachineType.h (the laptop copy has no `#define W906_PCI1203_IO_THREAD` block -- taking it would switch the IO thread off, against EastSun 1006 #128); uhome.cpp (TRAYSAFE-3: the same code line, different comment). uhome's other laptop hunks (HOME1530-SIM) are SOFT_SIMULTE only. 8 files back to the machine's CRLF.

o2 full build 0 errors; ctest 383/402 (Security_JamMerge failed under -j6, passes alone; the rest = the known list); production_audit baseline re-snapshotted 16:32, ctest 16:43-16:45, every change was written by EastSun's F5 started 16:45:32 (BootLog WinMain Enter) -- ctest wrote nothing; Debug wb_serve 16:45 (EastSun's F5 build, includes this package), release 16:51. WORKLOG section 3 row 160.

